{% doc %}
  Editor-only hint for unfinished content. Renders a dashed box only while the
  store is being edited or previewed: the theme editor, the editor's visual
  preview, or an unpublished or development theme. In production it renders
  nothing, so unfinished content can never ship to customers.

  Fail-closed: if the signals are missing or change, the hint stays hidden.
  `theme.role` is deprecated by Shopify, so it is only ever used to ADD preview
  contexts, never to decide that something is safe to show.

  The label is editor-facing English and intentionally not translated: it
  never reaches a customer.

  @param {string} label - What the merchant should do here
  @param {boolean} [wide] - Use the tall variant for section-sized gaps

  @example
  {% render 'placeholder', label: 'Hero: choose an image and add blocks', wide: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign preview = false
  if request.design_mode or request.visual_preview_mode
    assign preview = true
  elsif theme.role == 'unpublished' or theme.role == 'development'
    assign preview = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if preview -%}
  <div class="placeholder{% if wide %} placeholder--wide{% endif %}" role="note" data-placeholder>{{ label }}</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .placeholder { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 4rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px dashed var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius); color: var(--color-muted); font: 0.75rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); text-align: center; }
  .placeholder--wide { min-height: 12rem; }
{% endstylesheet %}
